# Line endings, and the files that must not have any applied to them.
#
# Git for Windows ships with `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this file a clone
# made there rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout. Biome formats to LF
# and `biome ci` compares against what it would write, so that clone fails the
# lint of every file it holds, for a reason nothing in the diff shows. The
# working tree is LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Content-addressed fixtures written by the Rust implementation. The bytes *are*
# the test — a hash is what the assertion compares — so Git must copy them
# through unexamined rather than trust its own text detection.
packages/core/src/storage/__fixtures__/rust-written-library/originals/** -text
packages/core/src/journal/__fixtures__/rust-written-journal/*.jsonl -text

# The conformance library (ADR-0052). RL-48 requires LF with no BOM, and the last
# line of a journal is deliberately truncated with no trailing newline. A checkout
# that "fixed" either would turn the fixture into a test of Git's settings.
conformance/library.roost/**        -text
conformance/made-before-the-rule/** -text

# Assets, and the SQLite databases a test may write beside them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gz binary
*.db binary
